<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zacatecas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zacatecas is a city in north-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> founded after the discovery of rich <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> deposits in 1546. It became one of the most productive silver-mining centres of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> cite the mines of Zacatecas, alongside those of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potosi">Potosí</a>, as sources of the American silver that financed the empire and flowed into the global economy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zacatecas.jpg" alt="Zacatecas" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ErickBasM · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Campo_en_zona_arqueol%C3%B3gica_La_Quemada.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
